<title>AUSTRIA: Wiener Staedtische '96 premiums up.</title>
<headline>Wiener Staedtische '96 premiums up.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian insurer Wiener Staedtische said on Thursday 1996 premium income had risen nine percent to a preliminary 17.3 billion schillings, citing strong demand for life insurance products.</p>
<p>Premiums on life insurance products alone rose 27 percent to 6.6 billion schillings, the insurer said.  </p>
<p>Damage and accident insurance premiums rose 1.2 percent to 7.5 billion schillings, while health insurance premiums fell 1.5 percent to 3.2 billion, it added.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
